db/ref 17592186386249 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186092399 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386514 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186092401 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386521 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186092530 1068 #edb/ref 17592186089321 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186092530 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387235 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186092530 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186092530 1071 "Construct the matrix of the linear transformation that acts on a vector in $R^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it rotates the vector by $\\frac{5π}{4}$ radians clockwise about the origin, and then\n- stretches the result by a stretch factor of $\\frac{1}{6}$ parallel to the $x$-axis." 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186092530 1071 "Construct the matrix of the linear transformation that acts on a vector in ${R}^{2}$ as follows (in the order given):\n\n- it rotates the vector by $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ radians clockwise about the origin, and then\n\n- stretches the result by a stretch factor of $\\frac{1}{6}$ parallel to the $x$-axis." 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186092530 1074 "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the rotation and let $Q$ be the matrix that represents the stretch. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{5\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $QP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QP & =(\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}])(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096637 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386723 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096639 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386736 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096659 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387007 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096680 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388243 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096681 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386215 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096702 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386902 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096704 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386909 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096704 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386916 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096752 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388250 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096767 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386805 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096767 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386895 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096800 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387014 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096816 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386798 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096823 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386763 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096823 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386770 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096844 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387394 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096845 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387408 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096845 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387415 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096845 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387436 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096846 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387422 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186096846 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387429 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186097019 1068 #edb/ref 17592186094057 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186097019 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386882 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186097019 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186097019 1074 "The vertex of a left-opening parabola is the right-most point of the parabola.\n\n![](images/94/94d33dcb92ddb84479c1ea7b01d5619268a10786a19f318fba61f3107ba9b551.png)\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(6,4).$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186100897 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387615 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186101137 1068 #edb/ref 17592186098127 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186101137 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388348 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186101137 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186101137 1071 "Find $(A + B) - C - (B - C)$, if\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186101137 1071 "Find $(A+B)-C-(B-C)$, if\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186101137 1074 "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)-C-(B-C) & =A+B-C-B+C \\\\  & =A+\\cancel{B}-\\cancel{C}-\\cancel{B}+\\cancel{C} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single matrix. So, the result is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105708 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387677 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105709 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387684 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105716 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386716 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105734 1038 #edb/ref 17592186385978 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105793 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386235 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105821 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386784 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105821 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386791 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105861 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387760 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105878 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386875 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105902 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387670 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186105903 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387726 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106033 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102054 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186106033 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386229 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106033 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106033 1071 "Consider the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+6y+8z=12 \\\\ y-z=-1 \\\\ 4x+4y+24z=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106033 1071 "Consider the system\n${2x + 6y + 8z = 12; y - z =-1; 4x + 4y + 24z = 7$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186106033 1074 "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 8 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 24 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 8 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 24 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 24 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 8 & -17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -25\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106048 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102144 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186106048 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387733 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106048 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106048 1071 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $x^{2} + y^{2} = 9$. Find the outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$." 13194139533462 17592186045585 false] [17592186106048 1071 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9.$ Find the outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186106048 1074 "We can parameterize $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi )\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation).\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n||{r}^{′}(t)||=\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}=3,\n$$\n\nand since for our curve $x(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ it follows that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186110574 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386847 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186110578 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386854 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186110578 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386861 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186110591 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386868 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115188 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387021 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115232 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388096 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115235 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388117 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388138 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388145 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388152 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115250 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388159 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115250 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388166 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186115251 