39533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386054 1071 "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3y=-x \\\\ 2y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386054 1072 #uuid "0f36e193-cfb7-556d-862d-7ca0f147ebca" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386054 1074 "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=0 \\\\ 2y=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386056 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386057 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386058 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386059 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386060 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386059 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386055 1080 #uuid "a482c228-62c7-528d-a980-052fac0d225f" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386056 1081 "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386056 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386056 1084 #uuid "cc295251-8992-58af-99ad-555c55679954" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386057 1081 "x=2[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386057 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386057 1084 #uuid "fa3e33dc-c2fa-5ce8-a74b-cafe4387cbba" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386058 1081 "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386058 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386058 1084 #uuid "afb508cc-f7c7-553c-b844-811d03f18621" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386059 1081 "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386059 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386059 1084 #uuid "38618689-5610-50ab-b2fe-e981dfe08e67" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386060 1081 "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386060 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386060 1084 #uuid "e35c6576-aa93-5aa2-bc00-3b5fc1b8c2d3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386061 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386062 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386061 1069 "q-103533" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386061 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386061 1071 "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=4.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386061 1072 #uuid "852dcdfe-ad8b-55fc-ab02-b3cb773c55c0" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386061 1074 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386063 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386064 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386065 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386066 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386067 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386066 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386062 1080 #uuid "e416161a-9bd1-5b5b-810d-ebf9a09026af" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386063 1081 "4[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386063 1084 #uuid "2e5a90ce-5f43-5f35-b7b8-583244a42439" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386064 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386064 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386064 1084 #uuid "8602540d-4801-5042-9916-98e607f58c64" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386065 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386065 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386065 1084 #uuid "c57393fc-dedc-5a9b-9994-032d00d28eef" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386066 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386066 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386066 1084 #uuid "8bc9fb87-d9dc-5a6b-ab93-485448959e7b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386067 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386067 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386067 1084 #uuid "66812ddb-563d-5415-bd8f-27772bb7e151" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386068 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386069 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386068 1069 "q-103776" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386068 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386068 1071 "The bacteria culture in a lab increases at a rate of ${e}^{2t}$ per hour. If, after $2$ hours, there are $2\\,000$ bacteria in the population, approximately how many bacteria are in the population after $6$ hours?" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386068 1072 #uuid "8de63944-9034-5911-a181-23fee9b4f403" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386068 1074 "Let $s(t)={e}^{2t}$ be the rate at which the number of bacteria is changing and let $S(T)$ be the total number of bacteria and in the population after $T$ hours.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nS(T)=S(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(T) & =S(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\,000+{\\int }_{2}^{T}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}{|}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2T}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2T}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of bacteria in the culture after $T=6$ hours, we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\nS(6)=2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\cdot 6}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}=2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{12}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}≈83\\,350.\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386070 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [1759218