 17592186045585 true] [17592186386083 1084 #uuid "ad573080-12c0-5795-bd57-186bf4ef86e9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386084 1081 "xy{e}^{xy}\\,i+(x+1){e}^{xy}\\,j" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386084 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386084 1084 #uuid "6637e684-fc51-5e28-9ef7-e989f843fa89" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386085 1081 "{y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\,i+{x}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\,j" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386085 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386085 1084 #uuid "bde9cf33-16b6-581e-a442-aa5532c2cea3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386086 1081 "(y+1){e}^{xy}\\,i+x{e}^{xy}\\,j" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386086 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386086 1084 #uuid "c7adf677-b962-5e7e-8a2d-2c8fa74b77c1" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386087 1081 "y{e}^{xy}\\,i+xy{e}^{xy}\\,j" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386087 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386087 1084 #uuid "8933c795-8d32-5777-bb3b-9769cea078c0" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386088 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386089 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386088 1069 "q-104425" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386088 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386088 1071 "![](images/d8/d869c61426504b7b24c2feebd60f68bca6f7dc8a2b40036bf5821e0208e1e197.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above. For what values of $x$ does the function $y=f(x)$ have a removable discontinuity?" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386088 1072 #uuid "12cf0cf4-20ea-574d-b3f6-b08a331df572" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386088 1074 "The function has a discontinuity at $x=2.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(2)=3$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=0$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)\\ne f(2)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=2$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nThe function also has a discontinuity at $x=5.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(5)=-1$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)=2$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)\\ne f(5)\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the third condition that failed, which tells us that $x=5$ is a removable discontinuity.\n\nFinally,  the function has a discontinuity at $x=-1.$ Checking our continuity conditions, we have:\n\n- $f(-1)=3$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)$ does not exists $\\,\\times $\n\nSo it's the second condition that failed, which tells us that $x=-1$ is not a removable discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $x=2$ and $x=5$ only." 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386090 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386091 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386092 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386093 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386094 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386094 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386089 1080 #uuid "2a91c606-abe7-5f5b-93f0-c007a89005ef" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386090 1081 "$x=-1$ and $x=2$ only" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386090 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386090 1084 #uuid "5efd41f4-a5c6-51c6-84dd-2ab8b7942847" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386091 1081 "$x=2$ only" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386091 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 1319413953346