2186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386142 1084 #uuid "cc92ac47-4627-58c3-a337-9804fd3c85cf" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386143 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386143 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386143 1084 #uuid "08ca37cb-d3b6-53e5-bdfa-41a6f5544e2a" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386144 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386144 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386144 1084 #uuid "bbae1fb7-89ca-5229-b719-b2c249fd8c2d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386145 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386145 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386145 1084 #uuid "6e9053ec-d943-5648-be8d-e9cc0c0fa69d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386146 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386146 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386146 1084 #uuid "130e27a8-0043-5a84-8507-122ce01fb961" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386147 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386148 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386147 1069 "q-105181" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386147 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386147 1071 "Which of the following functions is continuous on the interval $[1,4]?$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386147 1072 #uuid "f10cb2f1-287e-54d9-a68e-50d79d0f8000" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386147 1074 "The correct answer is the following. \n\n![](images/03/03d8fa6c421deebb49b3746425f799a2eea7fc22f07175bb1cf80d270f896555.png)\n\n  \n\nIndeed, this function is continuous on the open intervals $(-\\infty ,1)$ and $(1,5).$\n\nAdditionally, the function is right-continuous at $x=1.$ Hence, it is continuous on the interval $[1,5).$\n\nSo, we can say that the function is continuous on the intervals $(-\\infty ,1)$ and $[1,5).$ It is also continuous on any subinterval of these intervals.\n\nTherefore, this function is continuous on $[1,4]$ because $[1,4]$ is contained inside the interval $[1,5).$\n\nNotice that\n\n- $q(x)$ is not right-continuous at $x=1,$ so it is not continuous on the interval $[1,4].$\n\n- $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=2,$ and so it is not continuous on the interval $[1,4].$\n\n- $g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=3.$ So it is not continuous on the interval $[1,4].$\n\n- $p(x)$ is not defined at $x=4,$ and so it is not continuous on the interval $[1,4].$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386149 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386150 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386151 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386152 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386153 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386153 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386148 1080 #uuid "5d6e79ef-5309-5809-b54b-e5b877f96e8f" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386149 1081 "images/d5/d5cfd29b266bee94ed812edb71ac9804e385c9523341816be98ac278c088ef3b.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386149 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386149 1084 #uuid "3b055651-f48a-530d-8839-a9fa6a507120" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386150 1081 "images/f0/f0f65307224a5fea45530fd542be70d91039bc55aa2cd8b9f175378