#uuid "b53fb749-ec78-5073-8d2c-0d570e735c74" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386394 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{3}(3+2y-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}-8y+5}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386394 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386394 1084 #uuid "973ff8e0-c469-5352-83a3-899a50870ee3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386395 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{-2}^{4}(3+2y-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}+5}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386395 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386395 1084 #uuid "08d51801-95a0-5cf0-af42-9e6ca158940c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386397 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1069 "q-109254" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1071 "Consider the closed curve $C,$ which is the boundary of the region enclosed by the unit circle and the coordinate axes in the first quadrant. Express ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$  where $F(x,y)=⟨y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}}⟩,$ as a repeated integral." 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1072 #uuid "ec0b1748-e212-5d96-8358-0b705e724a9f" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386396 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](images/e4/e48034aed1f41cf1f9b30c057186879233fe05cd2ba720dcee436398a732b6ce.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx+(x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}})\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx+(x-{e}^{-{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386398 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386399 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386400 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386401 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386402 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386402 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386397 1080 #uuid "375112e1-4816-53a5-b797-a9ab4149ddab" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386398 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386398 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386398 1084 #uuid "e823e3a1-e75b-5988-a51e-22e31b8a9028" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386399 1081 "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true