nd{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix equation $(A-3I){v}_{2}={v}_{1}$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}-2{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get  \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $3a+6b=3\\cdot (-\\frac{5}{3})+6\\cdot 1=1.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386433 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386434 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386435 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386436 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386437 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386435 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386432 1080 #uuid "d67cfca8-f415-5451-865f-68e0a805ac21" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386433 1081 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386433 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386433 1084 #uuid "eeab0713-efb3-