⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,1,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,-1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,-1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386509 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386510 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386511 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386512 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386513 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386512 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386508 1080 #uuid "fe982dd6-a14a-54a1-8b75-39eeff47e074" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386509 1081 "⟨4,\\,2,\\,2⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386509 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386509 1084 #uuid "dbf84b3a-1cde-5413-97a8-b2616697d3c3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386510 1081 "⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386510 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386510 1084 #uuid "be51b9a8-5649-53a9-97ab-45900dff75c1" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386511 1081 "⟨-2,\\,4,\\,2⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386511 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386511 1084 #uuid "86ac33fd-5d35-527e-b07e-0f091da3a2f9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386512 1081 "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-2⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386512 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386512 1084 #uuid "b7c9ac4c-6c9b-5291-8404-cf6ec19ebab3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386513 1081 "⟨-4,\\,1,\\,2⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386513 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386513 1084 #uuid "1e3b28cd-c614-5056-9f3a-a31b14b6c3de" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386514 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386515 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386514 1069 "q-110203" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386514 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386514 1071 "The geometric series $2+4+8+16+32$ can be expressed using sigma notation as" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386514 1072 #uuid "8f23f3af-8d0d-56e0-9a43-df8749410139" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386514 1074 "First, we must express the given series in the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ denotes the first term of the series, $r$ denotes the common ratio, and $N$ denotes the number of terms in the series. In this case, ${a}_{1}=2$ and $N=5.$\n\nTo find $r,$ we calculate the ratio of the first two terms in the series:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{4}{2}=2\n$$\n\nHence, expressing the geometric series given in sigma notation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n2+4+8+16+32={\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}2\\cdot {2}^{n-1}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nFinally, we can simplify the above series using the laws of exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}2\\cdot {2}^{n-1} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}2\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}2\\cdot {2}^{-1}\\cdot {2}^{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{5}{2}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386515 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386