084 #uuid "b0a9dbae-7498-55b8-b00b-07a41ab70457" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386695 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386696 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386695 1069 "q-113513" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386695 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386695 1071 "Let $B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$  be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $S$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386695 1072 #uuid "4593a4d9-b03b-5c1f-ad85-95d87fe0ce9e" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386695 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $S$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{e}_{1},{e}_{2}}$, respectively. Recall that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $S$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386697 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386698 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386699 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386700 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386701 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386698 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386696 1080 #uuid "24689871-0c4d-593c-87fd-274e73d396ab" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386697 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386697 1084 #uuid "8825f14c-9a42-524d-9c28-29837aebedb6" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386698 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386698 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386698 1084 #uuid "98835778-342b-5c02-8d88-888de609e677" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386699 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386699 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386699 1084 #uuid "d94196f9-3ecd-5be0-83e8-bcc999375295" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386700 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386700 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [