uuid "6779086a-d9f7-527c-b7a2-fa6949f6719a" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386752 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386752 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386752 1084 #uuid "445a8ead-7ebd-5a64-951d-ab15b08684f2" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386753 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386753 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386753 1084 #uuid "4628885e-6385-5ab3-b41b-a525474e257a" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386754 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386754 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386754 1084 #uuid "9dd51d41-7edf-5ba3-afa4-a7eb672d5019" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386755 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386755 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386755 1084 #uuid "7afe6585-c10f-5041-a009-55754b363ba5" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386756 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386757 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386756 1069 "q-11487" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386756 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386756 1071 "Which integral gives the area of the finite region bounded between $y={x}^{2}-5$ and $y=4x?$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386756 1072 #uuid "dd8d0f5b-37a6-5193-9c93-2abd275a5141" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386756 1074 "First, let's draw a sketch of the two functions.\n\n![](images/b2/b25bee7ef7257a5611d708eb65b3c8b453b230ad6d2e9289f6cb40dffba89277.png)\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*\n\nNow, we want to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we equate the two functions and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & ={x}^{2}-5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x-5 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=-1$ to $x=5.$\n\nTo determine which is the lower function and which is the upper, let's draw our vertical arrow.\n\n![](images/bf/bf79cec9c1ede4a95b3e20415fbf37224ca8616426e8530043fa4a4b54780bab.png)\n\nThe vertical line \n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y={x}^{2}-5,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=4x.$\n\nTherefore, the integral that gives our area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5}[\\,(\\text{upper function})-(\\text{lower function})\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5}[\\,(4x)-({x}^{2}-5)\\,]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5}(-{x}^{2}+4x+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{5}(5+4x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386758 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386759 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386760 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386761 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386762 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1079 #edb/ref 17592186386759 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386757 1080 #uuid "182a2de1-8101-5395-96f9-70402cec0f5c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386758 1081 "{\\int }_{-2}^{4}(5+4x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386758 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386758 1084 #uuid "fde940dc-e573-5e35-8fd2-9c252d6ce798" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386759 1081 "{\\int }