369d621a6c2d06b4db1485ff43f6af4be2014e9d26564c9ca11e9bd38cd.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386922 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386922 1084 #uuid "6f16a9da-248f-5eb6-9d9c-67a9d932876b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386923 1068 #edb/ref 17592186386924 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386923 1069 "q-119184" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386923 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386923 1071 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-x?$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386923 1072 #uuid "4db1550d-68e2-55f5-aa48-87d9e6b19e56" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386923 1074 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,2),(-2,-1)$ and $(2,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,2)}=1-(-2)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-1)}=1-(-2)=3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=1-2=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following:\n\n![](images/91/911af9ca268f5f4c9cbac7b9c063eae54defce6d99dfadef609892b93ad58ae4.png)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386925 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386926 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386927 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386928 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186386929 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386924 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186386924 1077 "selection" 13