ef 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387012 1084 #uuid "748b1bc5-d773-5fa4-a285-111048597c9c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387013 1081 "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{8}h+\\frac{5}{8}i" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387013 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387013 1084 #uuid "86f8cb36-0676-5c61-8d2f-37ebe1006578" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387014 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387015 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387014 1069 "q-12049" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387014 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387014 1071 "![](images/2f/2f9e6eff196e24ddabca8d778d27e499fc1b856ef7169257a31a7cbaca8b564b.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TP}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{TS}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RS}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387014 1072 #uuid "b958283a-525c-51ab-a33e-68049ee3df0d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387014 1074 "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e1d5eb2f392332f69fa1507899b30b838a42ebd1c40dacddeca4edcf0f7aa8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=-b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](images/0e/0e8e24968141284550fac7d4e5c63333789f30ade8f7d5dd8b87fae4e012673a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =a+(-b) \\\\  & =a-b\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387016 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387017 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387018 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387019 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387020 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387018 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387015 1080 #uuid "80e3c074-2fe2-56ad-8be9-99fa6a58e9b4" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387016 1081 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b-c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387016 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387016 1084 #uuid "60fa9802-8c91-55e9-84a5-e1363e2e7308" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387017 1081 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b+c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387017 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387017 1084 #uuid "9d30e4cd-7866-5dc8-9d17-e3603b0e1d04" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387018 1081 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a-b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387018 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387018 1084 #uuid "0e6b1f27-9577-571f-a402-5318532c66a7" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387019 1081 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a+b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387019 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387019 1084 #uuid "6efc2e18-f131-54ef-8b65-97d65d26fb87" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387020 1081 "\\overset{\\to }{QT}=a+d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387020 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387020 1084 #uuid "4939a251-4f3d-5483-a371-05ba68aaf27c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387021 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387022 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387021 1069 "q-120532" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387021 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387021 1071 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+3=-1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387021 1072 #uuid "398ff4f2-a514-55ba-ad0a-235934ea5e85" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387021 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+3 & =-1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value: \n\n$$\nx=\\text{arcsin}(-\\frac{1}{2})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{∘}.$ \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=x+{360}^{∘}=-{30}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={330}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo,  our first solution is ${x}_{1}={330}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$\n\n![](images/b3/b3c523e882baf0b3a105e10131091e40de686b4c1483f46e7bdc235e30743a6d.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x={210}^{∘},{330}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=210\\cdot 330=69\\,300.