 $t=1,$ calculate the position vector of $P$ at time $t.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387200 1072 #uuid "daf2173d-c92c-5783-9142-5642bf903eb2" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387200 1074 "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector. To find the velocity vector, we first need to integrate the acceleration vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},0⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})\\text{d}t,\\int 0\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t}+{C}_{1},{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=⟨1,-1⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{1}+{C}_{1},{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨1,-1⟩ & =⟨1+{C}_{1},{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=0$ and ${C}_{2}=-1.$ Therefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the position vector by integrating the velocity vector.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{t},-1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (-1)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+{C}_{3},-t+{C}_{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(1)=⟨2,3⟩.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{C}_{3},-1+{C}_{4}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2,3⟩ & =⟨{C}_{3},-1+{C}_{4}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{3}=2$ and ${C}_{4}=4.$ Therefore, the position of $P$ at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,4-t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387202 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387203 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387204 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387205 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387206 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387204 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387201 1080 #uuid "62463180-a575-5094-bd92-23503f886ae4" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387202 1081 "r(t)=⟨2+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,3t⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387202 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387202 1084 #uuid "ef9fabf9-c18c-50a1-963a-7448f08bf2a0" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387203 1081 "r(t)=⟨2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,5t-2⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387203 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387203 1084 #uuid "846cf632-7b3a-5114-8f92-b6680d7ea90d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387204 1081 "r(t)=⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,4-t⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387204 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387204 1084 #uuid "4a4d7265-d9e7-543f-b5ac-4cb4a42855c6" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387205 1081 "r(t)=⟨2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,4-t⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387205 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387205 1084 #uuid "169de5da-2a43-5074-932b-ff3949f05195" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387206 1081 "r(t)=⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,5t-2⟩" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387206 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387206 1084 #uuid "10fab286-e298-5bb7-b569-1f7e5bfc15e2" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387207 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387208 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387207 1069 "q-122476" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387207 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387207 1071 "How many $5$-letter words (legitimate or made-up) can be made using the letters of the word ALGORITHMS, where each letter cannot appear in the word more than once?" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387207 1072 #uuid "8f3b348f-3d24-534c-8714-77102243eca3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387207 1074 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $10$ different letters in the word ALGORITHMS, so $n=10.$ We want to select $5$ of those letters to make a $5$-letter word, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different made-up words is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{10}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{10!}{(10-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30\\,240.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387209 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387210 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387211 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387212 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387213 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387212 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387208 1080 #uuid "3f3ce0b2-9f8b-54dc-a549-62477751c6e8" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387209 1081 "151\\,200" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387209 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387209 1084 #uuid "259822a5-969c-59bd-9409-203032b8e5c4" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387210 1081 "3\\,024" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387210 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387210 1084 #uuid "3abdd947-03f1-5fe3-acea-f4487dafdafc" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387211 1081 "100\\,000" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387211 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387211 1084 #uuid "16948774-922d-5453-867e-9d6ae6b1b44d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387212 1081 "30\\,240" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387212 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387212 1084 #uuid "a3a7f2b7-c75d-5c1f-8bac-5e57c8a4dbd9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387213 1081 "120" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387213 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387213 1084 #uuid "e8cb95f4-d026-5528-8f18-e7dc00345196" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387214 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387215 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387214 1069 "q-122540" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387214 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387214 1071 "Which of the following gives the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=1-{y}^{2},$ traversed once along the circle $C$ with equation $(x+3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387214 1072 #uuid "0c026636-3333-5149-910a-9646132297e7" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387214 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a circle of radius $1$ centered at $(-3,0).$ It can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=1-{y}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =1-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2} \\\\  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387216 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387217 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387218 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387219 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387220 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387217 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387215 1080 #uuid "62bd1f76-c0c6-5efb-a8ef-61be55142b02" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387216 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387216 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592