es:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\,i+2y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-4,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(3,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-4,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,-1) & =i+2\\cdot (-1)\\,j=i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/14/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387271 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387272 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387273 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387274 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387275 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387271 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387270 1080 #uuid "07a54f60-4401-5cf2-ba14-b1330ea47fc2" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387271 1081 "images/14/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387271 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387271 1084 #uuid "2c7d1d36-652e-5181-9302-abbb5df8798b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387272 1081 "images/ac/acb20