& =2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\,i+2xy\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,1),$ $(2,1),$ and $(-2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,1) & ={1}^{2}\\,i+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 1\\,j=i-4j \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & ={1}^{2}\\,i+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+4\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-2,-1) & =(-1)^{2}\\,i+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-1)\\,j=i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/02/020c3ec7cd0e5e57bb4c6de8516988187c9038d9e5598b116966b71fa8b917d8.png)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387278 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387279 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387280 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387281 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387282 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387281 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387277 1080 #uuid "c39f6b60-6db1-56ec-93e1-e634b438a208" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387278 1081 "images/0c/0c425b6fcb88f4c958a7c0371a64a815eda5ebf8ed14b0adc06875de1e24003b.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387278 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387278 1084 #uuid "bec373fa-27cc-5734-871a-ec77749ea6a0" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387279 1081 "images/af/af7fdf48d36f477174867761b90d9349344029980012f1f7907f544efd3893bc.png" 13