semiaxes of $7$ and $2,$ respectively. Therefore, it can be parametrized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45{sin}^{2}⁡t+4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45{sin}^{2}⁡t+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{y},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{2(7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=7\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{2x}{y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }7\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\sqrt{45{sin}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =7{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\sqrt{45{sin}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387333 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387334 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387335 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387336 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387337 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387332 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387332 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [1759218638