2186387469 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ u+3v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(6,-5).$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387471 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387472 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387473 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387474 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387475 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387475 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387470 1080 #uuid "a8195c7e-2439-578b-8152-7320d6f74a0d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387471 1081 "(-6,-5)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387471 1083