y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe curve $C$ is a part-circle of radius $2$ centered at $O.$ It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le t\\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot {e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }f(r(t))\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot {e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387478 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387479 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387480 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387481 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387482 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387479 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387477 1080 #uuid "1a48ec71-cabe-53f3-8125-9985126072d7" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387478 1081 "4{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139533462 1759218604