ne under the action of $T?$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387532 1072 #uuid "4e2708ca-fcbe-50bf-9e70-d85bebde1bc3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387532 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v+1 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](images/c8/c89be48140d49ce8c9def44122aa2bfac779bdd02cfbfbe98f97d414a5637409.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our square:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(1,1),(3,2),(1,0),$ and $(-1,-1).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](images/d0/d038caec0aa360e5d8cc1bcb4a3aa4d88408496d947b312d47634e51bbf4a11f.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-1<0,$ this transformation is not orientation-preserving." 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387534 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387535 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387536 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387537 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387538 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387537 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387533 1080 #uuid "a38e67bb-e34c-55bf-a3c2-118ea414d5d9" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387534 1081 "images/e4/e4ab9f75402ccf20fa66cd08f910d8afed0314e063b835f4697450e595fbc3fe.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387534 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387534 1084 #uuid "d0517751-be50-56a6-87a6-c1c8c1b63a53" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387535 1081 "images/c1/c1219b3ee5d914ab1f202d337fe16ef1dc19ac654ddf8e214b01b9d58fb3633d.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387535 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387535 1084 #uuid "03d620f7-2005-562d-962e-5d74b362b8f8" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387536 1081 "images/a3/a3c550025c6f5e7d5227f3ec1ce3ddf9a5efb20531217fdcb9bed5605e7c36e3.png" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387536 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186