m\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x$ and $a=1.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ f(1) & =(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi =-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x-\\pi x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi x \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -(1)\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi =-1+0=-1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi x-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi x-{\\pi }^{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x=-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi x-{\\pi }^{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi =0+{\\pi }^{2}={\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x & =-1-(x-1)+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2!}(x-1)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =-1-(x-1)+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}(x-1)^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387755 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387756 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387757 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387758 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387759 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1079 #edb/ref 17592186387756 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387754 1080 #uuid "4e410776-5a5d-52d6-9b3d-5e4832165ce3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387755 1081 "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x=-1+\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{3}(x-1)^{2}+⋯" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387755 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387755 1084 #uuid "88a8ae4a-7d9a-5bad-99ab-74b142493eb3" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387756 1081 "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x=-1-(x-1)+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}(x-1)^{2}+⋯" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387756 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387756 1084 #uuid "81d45b45-5be1-51e6-ba2b-63a22cc0f119" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387757 1081 "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x=(x-1)-(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387757 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387757 1084 #uuid "3e27ea36-90d3-578c-bb42-bda7cb9fba3c" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387758 1081 "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x=-1+2(x-1)-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}(x-1)^{2}+⋯" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387758 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387758 1084 #uuid "5abeb472-bc3e-5679-a043-fb244eebbd94" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387759 1081 "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x=(x-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387759 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387759 1084 #uuid "9d667c7c-80eb-553e-9e58-a2dc19802c21" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387760 1068 #edb/ref 17592186387761 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387760 1069 "q-126918" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387760 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387760 1071 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16.$ Find the outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387760 1072 #uuid "568e518b-6dee-5582-961d-6548648b3418" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387760 1074 "We can parameterize $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\nr(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi )\n$$\n\nTo calculate the outward-pointing normal vector of a closed, positively oriented curve, we follow three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: We compute the tangent vector ${r}^{′}(t).$\n\nDifferentiating the expression for $r(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Since $C$ is oriented counterclockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *clockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation).\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n||{r}^{′}(t)||=\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}=4,\n$$\n\nand since for our curve $x(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ it follows that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387761 1075 #edb/ref 17592186387762 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186387761 1075 #edb/ref 17592