a-8318-f1384fd1027b" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388229 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2}z & xz & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z)]k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)i-(0-{x}^{2})j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j+z\\,k+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{z}^{2}\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+({x}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\,j+(z-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F+G))(0,1,2)=-4\\,j+2\\,k.\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388231 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388232 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388233 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388234 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388235 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388230 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388231 13194139533462 17