569bfc8bc49d3.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type II regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y-2\\le x\\le 0}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-2\\le x\\le 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y-2\\,⟹\\,y=x+2,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=-y-2\\,⟹\\,y=-x-2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x-2\\le y\\le x+2},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/ba/ba9c9132c8efdb811e63bebc05e1f46bc8cbc54bcb8246072013a75d53bcb4df.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388294 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388295 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388296 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388297 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388298 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1077 "selection" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1079 #edb/ref 17592186388298 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388293 1080 #uuid "53604b27-d02f-579a-aedc-0bb673c96dd1" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388294 1081 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388294 1083 #edb