 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388306 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388306 1072 #uuid "446a02c7-d043-54a5-9d35-72c77f70ee6d" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388306 1074 "![](images/e6/e6b8889f9e8025cfca1ee0ae61b67a2f7ec9ec4aee15fab78d2f418a655bbcb8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le 1-y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](images/52/52640b30ded8bf2cd19fe7860c7640bde3c8427ae8978f32fb8020b2f7215468.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=1-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x+1}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388308 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388309 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388310 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388311 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388307 1075 #edb/ref 1759218638