d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388312 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388312 1084 #uuid "1bd1906e-d666-5eb2-a038-16879750e5dc" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388313 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388314 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388313 1069 "q-133968" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388313 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388313 1071 "A teacher wants to determine whether a student's performance in mathematics influences their performance in physics. The following table shows the grades of $5$ students in a mathematics and physics class. \n\n| **Math Grade** | **$8$** | **$6$** | **$8$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Physics Grade** | $9$ | $5$ | $8$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388313 1072 #uuid "935951a4-ee2a-54bc-9e42-14a72505ef8e" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388313 1074 "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (math grade) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (physics grade) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/5b/5bdbaadf2d3ea794c145365f5ee61ee4c1551dc72b62c8a681933b9aac74d214.png)" 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388315 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388316 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388317 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388318 13194139533462 17592186045585 true] [17592186388314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388319 13194139